<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-rōdo</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>no perf.</i>,
				rōsum, 3, v. a., <i>to gnaw off</i> or <i>away</i>, <i>to consume.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vites (animalia),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 15, 52, § 146</span></i>
			; cf. frondes, Col. <b>poet.</b> 10,
			323.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen., <i>to eat away</i>, <i>corrode</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aes, ferrum (aqua),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 2, 19, § 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbores sale,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 9, 20, § 37</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Esp.
			in medic. lang., of <i>erosive</i> remedies, <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
			28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 24, 11, 52, § 89</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34, 15, 46, §
			176</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>